For varying values of "fun", of course.

At least one of those values arises from the use of "alternate victory
conditions"... which, while they can be enjoyable for some, should not
be directly considered when designing the game, and should be left up to
the players who don't wish to play to the primary victory condition.  In
Nethack, the primary victory condition is ascension.

When a circumstance arises that interferes with the design of the game
as taken from the viewpoint of the primary victory condition, the
defense "but it will change/make impossible my personal alternate
victory condition" is not valid.

Interestingly, Nethack even has intentionally-designed "official"
alternate victory conditions (conducts), but even those are subservient
to the primary victory condition, ascension.

